## Why This Is Asked
Testing rate limiting is a practical task that reveals understanding of HTTP status codes, headers, and client behavior under load.

## Key Concepts
- Per-user rate limits and isolation
- Retry-After semantics and clock drift
- JSON schema validation
- Concurrency and race conditions
- Auth impact on quotas

## Code Example
```javascript
// example: simple check skeleton using fetch
async function testRateLimit(apiKey){
  const url = '/search?q=foo';
  // loop up to limit
  for(let i=0;i<100;i++){
    const r = await fetch(url, {headers: apiKey? {'Authorization': 'Key '+apiKey}: {}});
    // collect status codes
  }
}
```

